2026-10-20T07:39:36.7515127Z [36;1m# Nightly runs sit on main; comparing against the commit before[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7515365Z [36;1m# the latest lets the drift gate re-verify the newest merge.[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7515604Z [36;1m# There is no fallback on purpose: `|| git rev-parse HEAD` used to[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7515839Z [36;1m# sit here, and a ref that resolves to HEAD compares the tree[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7516085Z [36;1m# against itself -- byte-identical by construction, so no drift can[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7516327Z [36;1m# ever be reported and every claim is stale. env_drift.py now[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7516555Z [36;1m# refuses that state; failing here instead says which step is at[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7516792Z [36;1m# fault. A root commit (no HEAD^1) is the only way to get here.[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7517048Z [36;1mREF=$(git rev-parse --verify --quiet 'HEAD^1^{commit}') || {[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7517298Z [36;1m  echo "HEAD has no first parent, so there is nothing to compare"[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7517531Z [36;1m  echo "this tree against. The drift gate needs a real baseline;"[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7517860Z [36;1m  echo "check out main with history (fetch-depth: 0) and re-run."[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7518042Z [36;1m  exit 1[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7518148Z [36;1m}[0m
2026-10-20T07:39:36.7518273Z [36;1mecho "GOLDEN_REF=${REF}" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"[0m
